const LEGAL={"terms": {"title": "Terms of Service", "html": "<p>Effective date: 25 October 2026</p>\n<p>These Terms govern your use of the Kodu website and apps (the Platform). Kodu is operated by [Kodu OÜ], registry code [00000000], [street address], Tallinn, Estonia (Kodu, we, us). By creating an account you accept these Terms. If you register as a service provider, the Provider Agreement also applies to you.</p>\n<h2>1. What Kodu does</h2>\n<p>Kodu is an online marketplace that connects people who need work done at home (Customers) with independent tradespeople and businesses (Providers) for plumbing, electrical work, painting, cleaning, handyman tasks and moving. Kodu offers search, translated chat, quoting, booking, payment handling and reviews.</p>\n<p>Kodu is not a party to the service contract between a Customer and a Provider. Each job is a contract directly between them. Kodu does not employ Providers, does not direct how they work and is not responsible for the work itself, except where these Terms or mandatory law say otherwise.</p>\n<h2>2. Who can use Kodu</h2>\n<p>You must be at least 18 years old and able to enter into binding contracts. You must give accurate information when you register and keep it up to date. One person may hold one Customer account and one Provider account. You are responsible for everything done through your account, so keep your password and verification code private.</p>\n<h2>3. Booking a job</h2>\n<p>A Customer describes the job, chooses a time slot and sends a request. The Provider may reply with a quote. A quote shows labour (hourly or fixed price), materials and the Kodu service fee as one total. A contract between the Customer and the Provider is formed when the Customer accepts the quote and pays. The price in an accepted quote does not change unless both sides agree a new quote in the app.</p>\n<p>If the Customer has told us that a landlord arranges repairs, Kodu may send the landlord the job description, the quote and the Provider profile so the landlord can approve it. The landlord never sees the chat.</p>\n<h2>4. Payment and escrow</h2>\n<p>Payments are processed by our licensed payment partner, [Stripe Payments Europe Ltd.]. Kodu never stores full card numbers. When the Customer pays, the money is held by the payment partner on behalf of the Provider until one of the following happens:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>the Customer confirms in the app that the job is done;</li>\n<li>72 hours pass after the booked slot without the Customer opening a dispute; or</li>\n<li>a dispute is resolved under section 7.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The money is then released to the Provider in full. The Kodu service fee of 10 percent is shown to the Customer in the quote and paid by the Customer as part of the total.</p>\n<h2>5. Cancellations</h2>\n<p>A Customer may cancel a request at no cost before paying. After paying, a Customer may cancel free of charge until 24 hours before the booked slot. Cancelling later costs a late cancellation fee of €15, which goes to the Provider; the rest is refunded. If the Provider cancels, the Customer receives a full refund.</p>\n<h2>6. Your right of withdrawal as a consumer</h2>\n<p>If you are a consumer, you have a legal right to withdraw from a service contract concluded online within 14 days. By booking a slot that falls inside those 14 days, you ask the Provider to start work before the withdrawal period ends. If you withdraw after work has started, you pay for the part already done. Once the work is fully performed, the right of withdrawal ends. This does not affect your rights if the work is faulty.</p>\n<h2>7. Problems with a job and disputes</h2>\n<p>If something goes wrong, open a dispute from the job page before the money is released. Kodu will hold the payment, ask both sides for information and photos, and propose a resolution, which may be a full release, a partial refund or a full refund. This process does not limit your statutory rights against the Provider for faulty work. Consumers may also bring a complaint to the Consumer Disputes Committee of the Estonian Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority, or to the courts.</p>\n<h2>8. Translation</h2>\n<p>Chat messages, requests and quotes are translated automatically by machine translation. Translations may contain mistakes. The original text is always shown under each translation and is the version that counts if there is a disagreement. Do not rely on a translation alone for safety critical instructions.</p>\n<h2>9. How results are ranked</h2>\n<p>Search results are ranked by: whether the Provider speaks one of your languages at level B2 or better, availability in your chosen slot, distance to your district, rating from Customer reviews, and reliability (the share of bookings started on time). Providers cannot pay for a higher position. Sponsored placements, if ever introduced, will be clearly labelled.</p>\n<h2>10. Reviews</h2>\n<p>Only Customers who have completed and paid for a job can review that Provider. Reviews must be honest and about the job. We do not edit reviews, but we remove reviews that break section 11. Ratings shown on profiles are averages of Customer reviews only.</p>\n<h2>11. What is not allowed</h2>\n<p>You must not: use Kodu for anything illegal; arrange to pay outside Kodu for a job found through Kodu in order to avoid the fee; post false, offensive or discriminatory content; harass other users; share another person's personal data without a reason; create fake accounts or fake reviews; or interfere with the security of the Platform.</p>\n<h2>12. Reporting illegal content</h2>\n<p>Anyone can report content they believe is illegal or breaks these Terms using the Report option on any profile, review or message, or by writing to [legal@kodu.ee]. We will confirm receipt, review the report diligently and tell you what we decided and why. If we remove content or restrict an account, we will explain the reason to the affected user, who may appeal through the app within six months.</p>\n<h2>13. Suspension and closing accounts</h2>\n<p>You can close your account at any time from Profile, Privacy and data. We may suspend or close an account that breaks these Terms, after giving reasons, and immediately where needed to protect other users. Open jobs and payments held in escrow are settled before an account is closed.</p>\n<h2>14. Liability</h2>\n<p>Kodu is responsible for running the Platform with reasonable care. Kodu is not liable for the work a Provider performs, for damage a Provider causes, or for what users say to each other, unless Kodu itself acted wrongly. Nothing in these Terms limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for intent or gross negligence, or any other liability that cannot be limited by law.</p>\n<h2>15. Changes to these Terms</h2>\n<p>We will tell you about material changes at least 30 days before they apply. If you do not agree, you may close your account before the changes take effect.</p>\n<h2>16. Law and courts</h2>\n<p>These Terms are governed by Estonian law. If you are a consumer living in another EU country, you also keep the protection of the mandatory consumer law of that country, and you may bring proceedings in the courts where you live.</p>\n<h2>17. Contact</h2>\n<p>[Kodu OÜ], [street address], Tallinn, Estonia. Email: [hello@kodu.ee]. Legal and content reports: [legal@kodu.ee].</p>"}, "privacy": {"title": "Privacy Notice", "html": "<p>Effective date: 25 October 2026</p>\n<p>This notice explains how Kodu handles personal data when you use the Kodu website and apps. The controller is [Kodu OÜ], registry code [00000000], [street address], Tallinn, Estonia. You can reach us at [privacy@kodu.ee].</p>\n<h2>1. What we collect</h2>\n<p><strong>Account data.</strong> Name, email, phone number, password (stored only as a hash), role (Customer or Provider), app language.</p>\n<p><strong>Profile data.</strong> Languages you speak and your level in each, city and district, home address, housing type, whether a landlord arranges repairs, and your landlord's name and contact details if you give them to us.</p>\n<p><strong>Provider data.</strong> Trade and job types, areas covered, prices, availability, licence or registration number, VAT number, trading form (sole trader or company), IBAN and payout preferences.</p>\n<p><strong>Verification data (Providers).</strong> Photos of an identity document, a selfie and a licence. These are checked by our verification partner and are deleted after the check; we keep only the result and the date.</p>\n<p><strong>Job data.</strong> Requests, descriptions, photos you upload, quotes, bookings, cancellations, disputes and reviews.</p>\n<p><strong>Messages.</strong> Chat messages and their machine translations.</p>\n<p><strong>Payment data.</strong> Payment status, amounts and the last four digits of a card. Full card details go directly to our payment partner and are never stored by Kodu.</p>\n<p><strong>Technical data.</strong> Device type, browser, IP address, log in times and, only if you agree, usage statistics.</p>\n<h2>2. Why we use it and on what legal basis</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n<th>Legal basis</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Creating your account, matching Customers with Providers, bookings, chat, translation, payments and payouts</td>\n<td>Performance of the contract (GDPR Art. 6(1)(b))</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Verifying Provider identity and licence</td>\n<td>Legitimate interest in keeping Customers safe (Art. 6(1)(f))</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sending the quote to your landlord when you ask us to</td>\n<td>Performance of the contract at your request</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bookkeeping, tax reporting under DAC7, anti money laundering checks by our payment partner</td>\n<td>Legal obligation (Art. 6(1)(c))</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Preventing fraud, fake reviews and misuse</td>\n<td>Legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f))</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Handling disputes and reports of illegal content</td>\n<td>Legitimate interest and legal obligation under the Digital Services Act</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tips for settling in Estonia and other marketing emails</td>\n<td>Consent (Art. 6(1)(a)), which you can withdraw at any time</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Analytics cookies</td>\n<td>Consent, see the Cookie Policy</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Data about your languages is used only to match you with Providers. We do not use it to infer nationality or ethnic origin, and we do not use any special category data.</p>\n<h2>3. Who sees your data</h2>\n<p><strong>Other users.</strong> Providers see a Customer's first name, languages and district before payment, and the full address only after payment. Customers see a Provider's public profile. A landlord you name sees the job, the quote and the Provider profile, never the chat.</p>\n<p><strong>Service providers acting for us.</strong> Payment processing [Stripe Payments Europe Ltd., Ireland]; identity verification [verification partner]; machine translation [translation provider]; hosting [hosting provider, EU region]; email and SMS delivery [provider]. Each works under a data processing agreement and only on our instructions.</p>\n<p><strong>Authorities.</strong> The Estonian Tax and Customs Board receives annual Provider earnings reports where the DAC7 thresholds are met. We share data with other authorities only where the law requires it.</p>\n<p>We do not sell personal data.</p>\n<h2>4. Transfers outside the EU</h2>\n<p>We aim to keep data in the European Economic Area. If a service provider processes data outside the EEA, we rely on an adequacy decision or the European Commission's standard contractual clauses, and you can ask us for a copy of the safeguards.</p>\n<h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Data</th>\n<th>Kept for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Account and profile</td>\n<td>While your account is open, then deleted within 30 days</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Identity documents and selfies</td>\n<td>Deleted after the verification check</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Jobs, quotes, payments and invoices</td>\n<td>7 years, as required by the Estonian Accounting Act</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Chat messages</td>\n<td>2 years after the last message in a conversation, longer only if part of a dispute</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Reviews</td>\n<td>While the Provider's profile exists; shown with your first name and initial only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Technical logs</td>\n<td>90 days</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>6. Your rights</h2>\n<p>You can ask to access, correct, delete or download your data, to restrict or object to its use, and to withdraw consent at any time. Most of this can be done in Profile, Privacy and data. Otherwise write to [privacy@kodu.ee]; we reply within one month. You also have the right to complain to the Estonian Data Protection Inspectorate (Andmekaitse Inspektsioon), Tatari 39, 10134 Tallinn, info@aki.ee, or to the authority in your own EU country.</p>\n<h2>7. Automated decisions</h2>\n<p>Kodu ranks search results automatically, as described in section 9 of the Terms of Service. Ranking does not have legal or similarly significant effects on you. Kodu does not make decisions about you based solely on automated processing that have such effects; account restrictions are always reviewed by a person.</p>\n<h2>8. Security</h2>\n<p>Data is encrypted in transit and at rest, access is limited to staff who need it, and payments are handled by a PCI DSS certified partner. If a breach is likely to put your rights at high risk, we will tell you without undue delay.</p>\n<h2>9. Children</h2>\n<p>Kodu is not for anyone under 18. We do not knowingly collect their data.</p>\n<h2>10. Changes</h2>\n<p>We will tell you in the app before any material change to this notice takes effect.</p>"}, "provider": {"title": "Provider Agreement", "html": "<p>Effective date: 25 October 2026</p>\n<p>This Agreement is between [Kodu OÜ], registry code [00000000], Tallinn, Estonia (Kodu) and you, the person or company offering services through Kodu (Provider). It applies together with the Terms of Service. If they conflict, this Agreement applies to you as a Provider.</p>\n<h2>1. Your status</h2>\n<p>You are an independent business. You decide whether to accept a request, what to quote, when you work and how you do the job. Nothing in this Agreement makes you an employee, worker or agent of Kodu. You are responsible for your own taxes, social contributions, insurance and permits.</p>\n<h2>2. Eligibility and verification</h2>\n<p>To receive bookings you must:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>be at least 18 and legally allowed to work in Estonia;</li>\n<li>pass identity verification through our partner;</li>\n<li>hold any licence or qualification your trade requires in Estonia, including electrical work qualifications where applicable, and keep it valid;</li>\n<li>register as a sole trader (FIE) or a company, and give us your VAT number if you are VAT registered; companies must provide a VAT number;</li>\n<li>give us a valid IBAN in your own or your company's name.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>You must tell us within 7 days if any of this changes. Kodu may pause your profile until checks are updated.</p>\n<h2>3. Your profile</h2>\n<p>Your profile must be accurate. Language levels must be honest: Customers rely on them. Prices, areas and availability must be kept current. Photos must be of your own work.</p>\n<h2>4. Quotes and jobs</h2>\n<p>A quote you send is a binding offer for the described job at the stated price, valid for 24 hours. You may not charge more than the accepted quote unless the Customer accepts a new quote in the app before the extra work. You must arrive at the agreed time, do the work with reasonable skill and care, follow safety rules, and photograph the finished work.</p>\n<h2>5. Fees and payment</h2>\n<p>Kodu charges the Customer a service fee of 10 percent of labour and materials. You receive the full quoted amount for labour and materials. Money is held by our payment partner until the Customer confirms the job, 72 hours pass after the slot without a dispute, or a dispute is resolved. Payouts are made weekly on Mondays free of charge, or within 30 minutes for a fee of 1 percent if you choose instant payout.</p>\n<h2>6. Cancellations and reliability</h2>\n<p>If you cancel a paid booking, the Customer is refunded in full and your reliability score falls. Repeated late cancellations or no shows may lead to your profile being paused. If the Customer cancels within 24 hours of the slot, you receive the €15 late cancellation fee.</p>\n<h2>7. Disputes</h2>\n<p>If a Customer opens a dispute you will be asked for your account and photos within 48 hours. Kodu decides how the held money is released and explains its decision. You keep your legal rights against the Customer.</p>\n<h2>8. Off platform payments</h2>\n<p>For 12 months after you are first introduced to a Customer through Kodu, you must not arrange to be paid outside Kodu for work with that Customer. Breaking this rule may lead to your account being closed.</p>\n<h2>9. Ranking</h2>\n<p>Your position in search depends on: languages you speak at B2 or better, availability in the requested slot, distance, rating and reliability. You cannot pay to rank higher.</p>\n<h2>10. Restriction, suspension and termination</h2>\n<p>Kodu will give you at least 30 days notice, with reasons, before ending this Agreement for convenience. Kodu may restrict or suspend your account earlier, with a statement of reasons, if you break this Agreement, the law or safety rules. You can appeal any restriction through our internal complaint process, which is free and answered within 14 days. You may also use mediation under the EU Platform to Business Regulation; our named mediators are [mediator name and address].</p>\n<h2>11. Tax reporting</h2>\n<p>Under EU rules (DAC7), Kodu reports to the Estonian Tax and Customs Board the identity and earnings of Providers who earn more than €2,000 or complete 30 or more jobs a year. You will receive a copy of the reported information each January.</p>\n<h2>12. Insurance and liability</h2>\n<p>You should hold public liability insurance suitable for your trade. You are liable to Customers for damage you cause and for the quality of your work. Kodu's liability towards you is limited to the fees Kodu earned from your jobs in the 12 months before the claim, except where the law does not allow a limit.</p>\n<h2>13. Data</h2>\n<p>You may use Customer details only to carry out the booked job. After the job you must delete any address or contact details you copied outside the app, unless you need them by law. Each side is a separate controller for the data it holds; see the Privacy Notice.</p>\n<h2>14. Changes</h2>\n<p>Kodu will give you at least 15 days notice of changes to this Agreement, or longer where the change requires you to make significant adjustments. You may end the Agreement before the change takes effect.</p>\n<h2>15. Law</h2>\n<p>This Agreement is governed by Estonian law. Courts in Tallinn (Harju County Court) have jurisdiction.</p>"}, "cookies": {"title": "Cookie Policy", "html": "<p>Effective date: 25 October 2026</p>\n<p>Kodu uses a small number of cookies and similar storage in your browser. We ask for your consent before using anything that is not strictly necessary, and you can change your choice at any time in Profile, Privacy and data.</p>\n<h2>Strictly necessary</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Name</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n<th>Kept for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>kodu_session</td>\n<td>Keeps you logged in</td>\n<td>Until you log out, at most 30 days</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>kodu_csrf</td>\n<td>Protects forms against cross site attacks</td>\n<td>Session</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>kodu_consent</td>\n<td>Remembers your cookie choice</td>\n<td>12 months</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>kodu.proto (local storage)</td>\n<td>Saves app state such as filters and drafts on your device</td>\n<td>Until you log out or clear it</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Analytics (only with consent)</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Name</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n<th>Kept for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>kodu_an</td>\n<td>Counts visits and which screens are used, without identifying you, so we can improve the app</td>\n<td>13 months</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>We do not use advertising or cross site tracking cookies.</p>\n<h2>Your choice</h2>\n<p>You can accept or refuse analytics in the cookie banner, change your mind later in the app, or block cookies in your browser. Blocking strictly necessary cookies will stop log in from working.</p>"}, "notice": {"title": "Legal notice", "html": "<p><strong>Operator:</strong> [Kodu OÜ]\n<strong>Registry code:</strong> [00000000], Estonian Commercial Register\n<strong>VAT number:</strong> [EE000000000]\n<strong>Address:</strong> [street address], Tallinn, Estonia\n<strong>Email:</strong> [hello@kodu.ee]\n<strong>Phone:</strong> [+372 0000 0000]</p>\n<p><strong>Single point of contact for authorities and users under the Digital Services Act:</strong> [legal@kodu.ee], in English or Estonian.</p>\n<p><strong>Data protection:</strong> [privacy@kodu.ee]. Supervisory authority: Estonian Data Protection Inspectorate, Tatari 39, 10134 Tallinn.</p>\n<p><strong>Consumer disputes:</strong> Consumer Disputes Committee, Estonian Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority, Endla 10a, 10122 Tallinn.</p>\n<p><strong>Payments:</strong> processed by [Stripe Payments Europe Ltd.], an authorised payment institution. Kodu does not hold customer funds itself.</p>\n<p><strong>Accessibility:</strong> we aim to meet WCAG 2.1 AA and the European Accessibility Act. Report barriers to [hello@kodu.ee].</p>"}};
SCREENS.legal=()=>{const k=S.legalDoc||"terms";const d=LEGAL[k];return `<div class="row" style="gap:10px;height:48px"><button class="ib" data-go="back" aria-label="Back">${ico("back")}</button><b style="font-family:Sora,sans-serif;font-size:18px">Legal</b></div>
<div class="row lchips" style="gap:8px;overflow-x:auto;margin:0 -20px;padding:0 20px">${Object.entries(LEGAL).map(([key,v])=>`<button class="chip ${key===k?"on":""}" data-legal="${key}">${v.title}</button>`).join("")}</div>
<div class="note">${ico("shield","#16201D",16)}<span>Prototype document for a university project. Names and codes in square brackets are placeholders and the text is not legal advice.</span></div>
<article class="legaldoc"><h1>${d.title}</h1>${d.html}</article><div style="height:24px"></div>`};
document.addEventListener("click",e=>{const t=e.target.closest("[data-legal]");if(!t)return;e.preventDefault();e.stopPropagation();S.legalDoc=t.dataset.legal;save();if(route==="legal"){render();const s=document.querySelector(".screen");if(s)s.scrollTop=0}else go("legal")},true);
